1
00:00:05,353 --> 00:00:07,373
You know your way around a sword.

2
00:00:07,793 --> 00:00:09,190
I'll grant you that much,

3
00:00:09,273 --> 00:00:12,390
but it will take much more
than mere ego if you think

4
00:00:12,473 --> 00:00:14,530
I'll be defeated by the time
the flames reach twelve.

5
00:00:14,613 --> 00:00:19,073
Your pride may well be your
undoing, mister...uh...who?

6
00:00:19,573 --> 00:00:20,403
Pardonnez-moi.

7
00:00:20,486 --> 00:00:22,473
We haven't been introduced yet.

8
00:00:22,953 --> 00:00:25,133
My name is Jean-Pierre Polnareff.

9
00:00:25,413 --> 00:00:27,153
Well met, Polnareff.

10
00:00:27,293 --> 00:00:29,290
It's good to know the
name of one's opponent.

11
00:00:29,373 --> 00:00:30,203
However...

12
00:00:35,833 --> 00:00:37,513
Back to the task at hand.

13
00:00:37,853 --> 00:00:40,270
If you're under the
assumption that my flames only

14
00:00:40,353 --> 00:00:43,090
burn upward or with the wind
as they would in nature,

15
00:00:43,173 --> 00:00:44,930
let me assure you they do not.

16
00:00:45,013 --> 00:00:49,425
My stand is named Magician's Red because
it wields fire as though by magic.

17
00:00:50,773 --> 00:00:53,910
Fire is what began life
itself in this world.

18
00:00:53,993 --> 00:00:58,413
I should have expected as much from
a fiery stand such as Magician's Red,

19
00:00:58,573 --> 00:01:00,102
who represents beginnings.

20
00:01:00,473 --> 00:01:03,753
However, you dare to
speak of pride and ego?

21
00:01:04,213 --> 00:01:08,553
I assure you that my
pride is well deserved!

22
00:01:16,573 --> 00:01:19,430
In the fraction of a second
that the coins lined up,

23
00:01:19,513 --> 00:01:23,090
he skewered all five of them
in a single shot! No. Huh?

24
00:01:23,173 --> 00:01:25,467
Why don't you take a look at him again?

25
00:01:26,293 --> 00:01:27,553
It can't be.

26
00:01:27,933 --> 00:01:29,910
There, stuck on the blade of his sword.

27
00:01:29,993 --> 00:01:32,993
He's cut a bit of flame
for every coin that he hit.

28
00:01:33,533 --> 00:01:37,053
Now you see that I'm every
bit as deadly as I had said.

29
00:01:37,273 --> 00:01:38,573
This is not mere ego.

30
00:01:39,033 --> 00:01:41,570
My stand has the unrestricted power to cut

31
00:01:41,653 --> 00:01:44,124
fire to ribbons as though it were nothing.

32
00:01:44,313 --> 00:01:48,453
It can slice through air, creating
a vacuum and guiding the fire.

33
00:01:48,773 --> 00:01:50,170
Your flames are useless.

34
00:01:50,253 --> 00:01:51,453
Face it,

35
00:01:51,713 --> 00:01:53,690
your magician's red may be fearsome,

36
00:01:53,773 --> 00:01:57,185
but it's powerless against the
likes of my silver chariot!

37
00:02:03,093 --> 00:02:04,333
How the devil?

38
00:02:05,053 --> 00:02:06,413
Victory and conquest.

39
00:02:06,593 --> 00:02:10,713
That represents the card, the
chariot, and defines my stand as well.

40
00:02:10,953 --> 00:02:14,650
I can beat you in this cramped little
place as well as anywhere else.

41
00:02:14,733 --> 00:02:16,170
Not very sporting, though.

42
00:02:16,253 --> 00:02:20,333
Your flames will serve you to greater
effect in a larger open space.

43
00:02:20,713 --> 00:02:23,310
Beating you at the apex
of your powers, Monsieur,

44
00:02:23,393 --> 00:02:25,687
is the only victory worthy of my stand.

45
00:02:29,373 --> 00:02:31,333
All of you, follow me outside!

46
00:03:02,773 --> 00:03:03,603
Thank you

47
00:03:03,686 --> 00:03:10,653
so

48
00:03:15,953 --> 00:03:16,783
much for watching.

49
00:03:16,866 --> 00:03:21,173
Thank you.

50
00:04:02,593 --> 00:04:05,133
What the hell kind of nonsense is this?

51
00:04:06,813 --> 00:04:10,253
I believe they call it
Tiger Balm Garden. Oh, yeah?

52
00:04:11,273 --> 00:04:12,913
Tiger Balm Garden,

53
00:04:13,153 --> 00:04:18,773
a fantastical hillside park built
along Hong Kong's famous Tai Han Road.

54
00:04:19,073 --> 00:04:24,053
With its surreal landscape of sculptures
and pagodas, it is a true Hong Kong oddity.

55
00:04:24,273 --> 00:04:26,813
A prediction, if I may indulge.

56
00:04:27,373 --> 00:04:30,193
Monsieur Avdol, you will die here.

57
00:04:30,753 --> 00:04:34,459
Destroyed by the flames of your
very own stand, Magician's Red.

58
00:04:36,933 --> 00:04:39,593
Avdol, Jotaro, this is not your fight.

59
00:04:40,633 --> 00:04:45,280
In an open space like this one, there's
nothing to keep my stand from fighting.

60
00:04:45,373 --> 00:04:46,453
at full force.

61
00:04:59,433 --> 00:05:00,393
En Card!

62
00:05:08,273 --> 00:05:09,273
Nothing at all?

63
00:05:09,493 --> 00:05:12,290
No sign of the flame you
were crying about before?

64
00:05:12,373 --> 00:05:13,233
Suit yourself!

65
00:05:13,553 --> 00:05:15,024
I shall press the attack!

66
00:05:29,793 --> 00:05:32,558
That goddamn bastard,
he's just toying with us!

67
00:05:32,873 --> 00:05:36,573
He used Magician's Reds on
fireballs to make a statue of it!

68
00:05:37,533 --> 00:05:38,593
Look at that.

69
00:05:40,113 --> 00:05:44,113
In a place this odd, I dare say
your fiendish face is right at home.

70
00:05:49,833 --> 00:05:51,793
Well, here it comes.

71
00:05:52,153 --> 00:05:56,741
Show me your true power at last, Avdol,
but know that it will never be enough.

72
00:05:56,913 --> 00:05:58,670
Hey, hide behind something already.

73
00:05:58,753 --> 00:06:00,210
Avdol's gonna blow his top.

74
00:06:00,293 --> 00:06:01,881
What are you talking about?

75
00:06:03,653 --> 00:06:04,483
Crossfire!

76
00:06:06,813 --> 00:06:07,643
Rikai!

77
00:06:11,193 --> 00:06:12,023
Really?

78
00:06:12,106 --> 00:06:13,270
Is that the best that you've got?

79
00:06:13,353 --> 00:06:15,533
I told you before what my sword does.

80
00:06:15,653 --> 00:06:19,829
It creates a gap between the pockets
of air so I can slice your flames!

81
00:06:28,113 --> 00:06:28,943
Abdel, no!

82
00:06:29,133 --> 00:06:32,773
The fire is so intense, it's
burning Stan and user alike!

83
00:06:38,013 --> 00:06:39,793
It's just as I foretold.

84
00:06:40,013 --> 00:06:43,553
You will die from an inferno
of your own making. Hmm?

85
00:06:45,433 --> 00:06:48,153
Good grief, just die already.

86
00:06:48,533 --> 00:06:51,239
One last pathetic gasp,
this is hard to watch.

87
00:06:53,313 --> 00:06:55,313
That hit felt wrong, what is this?

88
00:06:56,993 --> 00:06:57,823
What?

89
00:06:58,613 --> 00:06:59,443
Impossible.

90
00:06:59,553 --> 00:07:03,553
How can his stand injure me after
the moment of its own destruction?

91
00:07:04,173 --> 00:07:06,993
It's not the stand, you
bastard, it's a dummy.

92
00:07:09,693 --> 00:07:11,790
The flames blinded your eyes.

93
00:07:11,873 --> 00:07:16,713
What you really destroyed was the statue
that Silver Chariot carved earlier!

94
00:07:17,853 --> 00:07:20,090
Perhaps you didn't take
me at my word when I

95
00:07:20,173 --> 00:07:22,550
told you that I could
control my flames freely.

96
00:07:22,633 --> 00:07:26,770
When you deflected it, I used it to melt
the statue's joints and allow it to move.

97
00:07:26,853 --> 00:07:31,133
The one defeated by his own
stance powers is you, Polnareff!

98
00:07:31,673 --> 00:07:34,093
Now, let's try this again!

99
00:07:35,233 --> 00:07:36,973
Crossfire Hurricane! SHINE!

100
00:07:40,213 --> 00:07:44,389
Challenging a fortune-teller in a
battle of predictions is a bold move.

101
00:07:44,533 --> 00:07:48,357
Give it another decade and you
would have been a viable opponent.

102
00:07:50,233 --> 00:07:51,893
Such terrifying power!

103
00:07:52,233 --> 00:07:55,530
His stand must have melted in
the face of such an attack!

104
00:07:55,613 --> 00:07:56,443
It's done for!

105
00:07:56,573 --> 00:07:58,102
That's one hell of a burn.

106
00:07:58,293 --> 00:07:59,587
I'm betting he's dead.

107
00:07:59,753 --> 00:08:00,953
Or wishes he was.

108
00:08:01,493 --> 00:08:03,650
Yeah, he's not getting up from that.

109
00:08:03,733 --> 00:08:07,053
If he is alive, he'll be
flat on his back for months.

110
00:08:07,353 --> 00:08:10,059
Having your stand destroyed
is a major trauma.

111
00:08:11,193 --> 00:08:12,253
Now then, Mr.

112
00:08:12,413 --> 00:08:15,793
Joestar, let us resume
our trek to Egypt. Hmm.

113
00:08:24,353 --> 00:08:25,993
What the hell's going on?

114
00:08:26,133 --> 00:08:28,898
His stand just exploded
into a bunch of pieces!

115
00:08:31,453 --> 00:08:36,510
how is he still lying down but
suspended in midair bravo well

116
00:08:36,593 --> 00:08:41,850
done monsieur bravo that's impossible
I don't believe it he doesn't

117
00:08:41,933 --> 00:08:45,730
look injured at all yeah but
why the hell is he floating in

118
00:08:45,813 --> 00:08:51,753
the air look with your inner eye
and see the truth how can it be

119
00:08:54,073 --> 00:08:55,053
Out of control.

120
00:08:55,213 --> 00:08:56,272
Me well, monsieur.

121
00:08:56,773 --> 00:09:00,361
He may have shed his armor, but
it's still my silver chariot.

122
00:09:00,773 --> 00:09:03,293
You seem quite taken aback by this.

123
00:09:03,453 --> 00:09:05,990
I really should explain
before I destroy you.

124
00:09:06,073 --> 00:09:08,890
Otherwise, it wouldn't be
chivalrous, don't you agree?

125
00:09:08,973 --> 00:09:12,773
I'm sure you were expecting
nothing less, if you don't mind.

126
00:09:13,213 --> 00:09:16,493
May we take a short time
out for an explanation? Hmm.

127
00:09:17,153 --> 00:09:18,033
Very well.

128
00:09:18,573 --> 00:09:20,333
Let's hear this explanation.

129
00:09:22,013 --> 00:09:25,873
First, the explosion you saw was
not my stand self-destructing.

130
00:09:26,133 --> 00:09:29,093
What you took as Silver
Chariot's body was armor.

131
00:09:29,413 --> 00:09:30,933
Armor that was cast off.

132
00:09:31,193 --> 00:09:34,573
But before it did, it absorbed
the brunt of your flames.

133
00:09:34,853 --> 00:09:36,853
That's how I escaped further harm.

134
00:09:37,033 --> 00:09:40,393
And bereft of armor, it has
significantly more agility.

135
00:09:40,833 --> 00:09:43,773
Were you able to see my
stand as it held me up?

136
00:09:44,093 --> 00:09:44,933
That's right.

137
00:09:45,233 --> 00:09:47,998
Silver Chariot can now
move faster than before.

138
00:09:49,133 --> 00:09:49,963
Hmm.

139
00:09:50,046 --> 00:09:50,876
Illuminating.

140
00:09:50,959 --> 00:09:53,070
You're suggesting it only stood
there and took my crossfire

141
00:09:53,153 --> 00:09:56,270
hurricane head-on because the
armor didn't allow it to dodge,

142
00:09:56,353 --> 00:09:57,183
is that it?

143
00:09:58,273 --> 00:10:01,633
But bereft of armor, it is
also far more vulnerable.

144
00:10:02,073 --> 00:10:04,633
It may have survived
my attack once before,

145
00:10:04,853 --> 00:10:08,382
but if it were hit again, its
destruction would be absolute.

146
00:10:09,753 --> 00:10:10,773
That may be.

147
00:10:11,693 --> 00:10:12,523
Whee!

148
00:10:12,606 --> 00:10:13,593
How can one know?

149
00:10:14,513 --> 00:10:16,893
Such a shame, we'll never find out.

150
00:10:17,633 --> 00:10:18,463
Never, huh?

151
00:10:18,546 --> 00:10:20,713
Well, mind if I try it out?

152
00:10:20,933 --> 00:10:24,933
First, let me show you all something
that will really freak you out.

153
00:10:25,473 --> 00:10:26,813
Well, go ahead then.

154
00:10:27,673 --> 00:10:28,833
What the devil?

155
00:10:29,433 --> 00:10:33,973
He now has six, no, no wait, he
has a total of seven stands now.

156
00:10:34,493 --> 00:10:35,853
But that's impossible.

157
00:10:36,073 --> 00:10:38,426
There should only be one stand per user.

158
00:10:39,093 --> 00:10:40,950
Tell me, are you freaked out yet?

159
00:10:41,033 --> 00:10:42,473
These are after images.

160
00:10:44,653 --> 00:10:48,993
Perfect mirrors of the Silver Chariot,
Guaranteed to fool your senses.

161
00:10:49,493 --> 00:10:53,773
Your sight, your hearing, your senses
can't follow their movement. Ugh.

162
00:10:54,493 --> 00:10:57,313
How do you like
insultsmanship now, monsieur?

163
00:11:13,013 --> 00:11:14,633
Suffer my red bun!

164
00:11:23,953 --> 00:11:24,783
Ah!

165
00:11:25,393 --> 00:11:29,030
I told you that efforts to track
it would be in vain, did I not?

166
00:11:29,113 --> 00:11:32,466
You waste your flame on images
and spare the real threat.

167
00:11:38,253 --> 00:11:39,393
Striking at random.

168
00:11:40,333 --> 00:11:43,230
Desperation is not a good
look on you, my dear Abdo.

169
00:11:43,313 --> 00:11:45,842
He's going to exhaust
himself at this rate.

170
00:11:50,153 --> 00:11:50,983
Crossfire!

171
00:11:51,066 --> 00:11:51,896
Hurricane!

172
00:11:57,073 --> 00:11:59,093
Menon, menon, menon, menon, menon!

173
00:11:59,273 --> 00:12:01,050
Have you learned nothing at all today?

174
00:12:01,133 --> 00:12:05,113
You're a fool whose attacks will
not work on my stand! Now give up!

175
00:12:10,793 --> 00:12:11,623
Haptor!

176
00:12:11,706 --> 00:12:15,210
What precision, what lethal
efficiency, it's plain to see.

177
00:12:15,293 --> 00:12:18,705
His stand's ability has been
trained, and at great length!

178
00:12:19,113 --> 00:12:22,033
Hmm, I've spent the last
decade honing my skill.

179
00:12:22,333 --> 00:12:25,070
You had better hit me with
everything you've got,

180
00:12:25,153 --> 00:12:28,212
for I intend my next attack
to be the coup de grace.

181
00:12:28,553 --> 00:12:33,030
It's very chivalrous of you to keep giving
me fair warning about your next move.

182
00:12:33,113 --> 00:12:34,853
Your honor is unimpeachable.

183
00:12:35,433 --> 00:12:40,353
You've inspired me, thus I too will
give fair warning before my next attack.

184
00:12:42,053 --> 00:12:42,883
Really?

185
00:12:45,313 --> 00:12:47,530
varieties than the one
you've already seen.

186
00:12:47,613 --> 00:12:51,010
It's a flame in the shape of an
ankh but it need not remain whole.

187
00:12:51,093 --> 00:12:54,393
I can divide it into as
many pieces as I deem fit.

188
00:12:58,013 --> 00:13:00,393
Crossfire Hurricane Special!

189
00:13:03,553 --> 00:13:05,113
Try and dodge them!

190
00:13:05,493 --> 00:13:07,793
You're a fool, Abdaal, it's useless!

191
00:13:11,833 --> 00:13:13,430
Damn, they've got him covered!

192
00:13:13,513 --> 00:13:14,950
He's thought of everything!

193
00:13:15,033 --> 00:13:16,490
Naive, naive, naive!

194
00:13:16,573 --> 00:13:17,773
So very naive!

195
00:13:18,373 --> 00:13:22,753
I will wield this divided flame
against you precisely as I did before!

196
00:13:23,273 --> 00:13:24,103
Slice it!

197
00:13:24,273 --> 00:13:25,593
And hurl it back!

198
00:13:30,973 --> 00:13:31,803
What?!

199
00:13:40,713 --> 00:13:41,543
That's...

200
00:13:41,626 --> 00:13:44,313
that's the hole that was
dug by the flames earlier.

201
00:13:44,513 --> 00:13:46,553
Now I get it! It's clear to me!

202
00:13:46,713 --> 00:13:49,110
The first shot was a
setup and nothing more!

203
00:13:49,193 --> 00:13:52,210
Then he used the tunnel to hit
him with Crossfire Hurricane!

204
00:13:52,293 --> 00:13:57,293
Like I said, that attack can be divided
up into as many pieces as are called for.

205
00:14:05,693 --> 00:14:08,393
Burning is a painful
way to meet one's end.

206
00:14:08,573 --> 00:14:10,926
Take the knife and end it while you can.

207
00:14:28,233 --> 00:14:30,133
My conceit was my undoing.

208
00:14:30,333 --> 00:14:34,333
I couldn't picture his fire standing
a chance against my sword work.

209
00:14:35,513 --> 00:14:39,270
A slow death amid the flames is
no less than I deserve, monsieur.

210
00:14:39,353 --> 00:14:42,270
I challenged you to this duel
and you were the clear victor.

211
00:14:42,353 --> 00:14:44,753
I would not sully it with suicide.

212
00:14:45,313 --> 00:14:48,553
It would be cowardly to end it myself.

213
00:14:54,173 --> 00:14:57,879
Even in your final moments, you
conduct yourself with chivalry.

214
00:14:58,173 --> 00:15:02,750
How easy it would have been for you to
throw that knife into my unsuspecting back.

215
00:15:02,833 --> 00:15:07,304
Even while working for a devil like
Dio, you've carried yourself with honor.

216
00:15:07,493 --> 00:15:09,140
Your death would be a waste.

217
00:15:09,373 --> 00:15:10,203
Hmm?

218
00:15:10,853 --> 00:15:13,677
Something must have set
him down this dark path.

219
00:15:14,513 --> 00:15:15,343
Jojo.

220
00:15:15,733 --> 00:15:16,563
Gotcha.

221
00:15:19,253 --> 00:15:22,693
Those tentacles are so gross,
I can't even look at them!

222
00:15:23,053 --> 00:15:23,994
Come on, Jotaro!

223
00:15:24,253 --> 00:15:25,830
Just destroy the damn thing!

224
00:15:25,913 --> 00:15:27,560
Quit your bitchin', old man!

225
00:15:29,933 --> 00:15:30,763
There!

226
00:15:30,846 --> 00:15:34,850
Now that my grandson has pulled out
that flesh, bud, we can all be buddies!

227
00:15:34,933 --> 00:15:35,763
You get it?

228
00:15:37,173 --> 00:15:38,213
Hey, Kakuline.

229
00:15:38,813 --> 00:15:43,754
Don't people who make stupid puns all the
time get on your nerves, or is it just me?

230
00:15:45,953 --> 00:15:49,482
The Speedwagon Foundation
chartered a boat for us yesterday.

231
00:15:49,593 --> 00:15:52,593
With any luck, it's reached
the harbor ahead of us.

232
00:15:53,913 --> 00:15:55,073
We meet again.

233
00:15:56,253 --> 00:15:58,253
So what's on your mind, Polnareff?

234
00:15:58,593 --> 00:16:02,510
I never thanked you properly for
freeing me from Dio's mind control.

235
00:16:02,593 --> 00:16:05,370
Young Jojo is the one you
should be thanking here.

236
00:16:05,453 --> 00:16:06,806
Don't need your thanks.

237
00:16:07,853 --> 00:16:11,373
It appears your fine manners
are wasted on the likes of us.

238
00:16:13,293 --> 00:16:16,587
As you wish, I've no desire
to come off as heavy-handed.

239
00:16:16,953 --> 00:16:18,873
But I'm not quite finished here.

240
00:16:19,373 --> 00:16:23,753
Monsieur Joestar, I hope you'll indulge
my asking a very bizarre question.

241
00:16:24,113 --> 00:16:25,793
A bizarre question, you say?

242
00:16:26,553 --> 00:16:28,990
I noticed at the restaurant
yesterday that you

243
00:16:29,073 --> 00:16:31,550
never took off your
gloves even while eating.

244
00:16:31,633 --> 00:16:35,430
Tell me, your left hand wouldn't happen
to be a right hand under that glove?

245
00:16:35,513 --> 00:16:36,343
Huh?

246
00:16:36,426 --> 00:16:38,053
Is my left hand a right one?

247
00:16:38,613 --> 00:16:41,110
You weren't kidding
about the bizarre part.

